# Interactive first-run setup — hub / runner question flow

Both `slayzone-hub` and `slayzone-runner` share one gate (`canPrompt()`) and one
subroutine (`runInteractiveConfig()`). The bins differ only in *when* they decide
a value is missing and *which* fields they ask.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph GATE["canPrompt() — shared gate"]
        G{"stdin.isTTY<br/>AND not SUPERVISED<br/>AND not NONINTERACTIVE?"}
    end

    START([bin boot]) --> G
    G -- no --> SKIP["skip setup →<br/>resolve config as before<br/>(auto-gen / fail-fast)"]

    G -- yes --> KIND{hub or runner?}

    %% ---------- RUNNER ----------
    KIND -- runner --> R1{"joinToken set?<br/>(env / config.json)"}
    R1 -- yes --> SKIP
    R1 -- no --> R2{"hubUrl known<br/>AND creds stored?"}
    R2 -- yes --> SKIP
    R2 -- no --> RQ["ask fields:<br/>1 join token<br/>2 allowedRoots (default=cwd)<br/>3 name (empty→live hostname)"]
    RQ --> RUN

    %% ---------- HUB ----------
    KIND -- hub --> H1{"publicUrl set?<br/>(env / config.json)"}
    H1 -- yes --> SKIP
    H1 -- no --> HQ["ask field:<br/>publicUrl<br/>(empty→loopback only)"]
    HQ --> RUN

    %% ---------- SHARED SUBROUTINE ----------
    subgraph SUB["runInteractiveConfig()"]
        RUN["for each field: ask"] --> EMPTY{"answer empty<br/>AND no default?"}
        EMPTY -- yes --> DROP["skip field<br/>(not collected)"]
        EMPTY -- no --> COLLECT["apply default/transform<br/>→ collect value"]
        DROP --> MORE
        COLLECT --> MORE{more fields?}
        MORE -- yes --> RUN
        MORE -- no --> ANY{"any collected?"}
        ANY -- no --> SKIP
        ANY -- yes --> SEED["seed process.env<br/>(this run uses values)"]
        SEED --> SUMMARY["print summary"]
        SUMMARY --> CONFIRM{"Save to config.json?<br/>[Y/n] (Enter=yes)"}
        CONFIRM -- yes --> WRITE["updateSlayzoneConfig()<br/>atomic 0600 merge"]
        CONFIRM -- no --> RUNONLY["run-only<br/>(not persisted)"]
    end

    WRITE --> BOOT([resolver reads env+config → boot])
    RUNONLY --> BOOT
    SKIP --> BOOT
```

## Invariants the flow encodes

- **Gate first.** Non-TTY / `SLAYZONE_SUPERVISED=1` / `SLAYZONE_NONINTERACTIVE=1`
  → straight to the old path. Deploy path (piped stdio) never prompts.
- **Skip if already answerable.** Runner: a join token OR stored credentials.
  Hub: `publicUrl` already set. A persisted value stops being "missing" → no
  re-prompt next boot.
- **Empty + no default = skip that field.** So an unanswered runner name stays
  the live hostname, and an unanswered hub `publicUrl` stays loopback-only.
- **env is seeded regardless of the save answer.** The bin's normal env-first
  resolver is the single source of truth; the `[Y/n]` confirm only decides
  whether the values also persist to `<ROOT>/config.json`.

## Fields

| Bin | Field | Default | Empty answer |
|-----|-------|---------|--------------|
| runner | join token | — | skipped (nothing to persist) |
| runner | allowedRoots | launch dir (cwd) | accepts default |
| runner | name | live hostname (hint only) | skipped → resolves hostname live |
| hub | publicUrl | — | skipped → loopback-only tokens |
